### DevPulse Phase 2 requests. Open in IntelliJ and click the green arrow next to a request.
### Start the app first (DevpulseApplication). With devpulse.seed-demo-data=true the projects
### shop, chat, analytics already exist and fake apps send events for about 20 seconds.

### 1. Register a project  -> 201 Created + Location header
POST http://localhost:8080/api/projects
Content-Type: application/json

{ "id": "billing", "name": "Billing Service", "owner": "dave" }

### 2. Same request again -> 409 Conflict (then look at the audit trail, request 12)

### 3. Invalid request -> 400 with a message per bad field
POST http://localhost:8080/api/projects
Content-Type: application/json

{ "id": "Bad Id!", "name": "", "owner": "dave" }

### 4. List projects
GET http://localhost:8080/api/projects

### 5. One project -> 200, or 404 if it does not exist
GET http://localhost:8080/api/projects/billing

### 6. Send an event -> 202 Accepted (queued, processed a moment later)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/events
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "projectId": "billing",
  "service": "invoice-api",
  "severity": "ERROR",
  "message": "Timeout after 3021ms calling payment-gateway",
  "errorType": "TimeoutException",
  "attributes": { "env": "prod" }
}

### 7. Event for a project nobody registered -> 404
POST http://localhost:8080/api/events
Content-Type: application/json

{ "projectId": "ghost", "service": "api", "severity": "INFO", "message": "hello" }

### 8. Events of a project, errors only, newest first
GET http://localhost:8080/api/projects/shop/events?minSeverity=ERROR&limit=10

### 9. Incidents (activeOnly=true hides resolved ones)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/incidents?activeOnly=true

### 10. Acknowledge an incident: paste a real id from request 9
POST http://localhost:8080/api/incidents/PASTE-ID-HERE/acknowledge
Content-Type: application/json

{ "by": "dave" }

### 11. Resolve it (repeat to see 409: RESOLVED is a final state)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/incidents/PASTE-ID-HERE/resolve

### 12. Audit trail: shows PROJECT_REGISTERED and PROJECT_REJECTED rows (transaction propagation)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/audit?limit=20

### 13. Dashboard numbers
GET http://localhost:8080/api/stats
